  (In a Command Prompt on the offline PC)

   1 # Create a folder for the environment
   2 mkdir C:\doc_parser_env
   3
   4 # Extract the tarball (Assuming USB is E:)
   5 tar -xzf E:\doc_parser_env.tar.gz -C C:\doc_parser_env

  2. Set the offline cache paths:
  This tells the code to look at the USB for the AI models instead of trying to use the internet.

   1 set HF_HOME="E:\AI_Cache\huggingface"
   2 set DOCLING_MODELS_CACHE="E:\AI_Cache\docling"
   3 set EASYOCR_MODULE_PATH="E:\AI_Cache\easyocr"

  3. Activate and Run:

   1 # Activate the environment
   2 C:\doc_parser_env\Scripts\activate.bat
   3
   4 # Navigate to the code on the USB
   5 E:
   6 cd Zenith-Vault
   7
   8 # Launch the UI
   9 streamlit run app.py --browser.gatherUsageStats False

